hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3007","**\nNarrated to us Al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Jazari: Narrated to us 'Abd al-A'la, from Muhammad (who is Ibn Ishaq), narrated to us 'Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid and 'Ata', that Ibn 'Abbas (RA) used to say:\n\nMy brother narrated to me that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered the Ka'bah, he fell down between the two pillars in prostration, then sat and supplicated, and did not pray."
